From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: mxsimage: honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

sb_get_timestamp() reads the wall clock, and sb_prefill_image_header()
writes the value to the timestamp of the boot image header. The header
digest covers that field, so a .sb image built twice from the same input
differs in both.

Use imagetool_get_source_date(), which the other image tools already use,
and keep the wall clock as the fallback.

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
---
 tools/mxsimage.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/mxsimage.c
+++ b/tools/mxsimage.c
@@ -289,7 +289,8 @@ static time_t sb_get_timestamp(void)
 		.tm_year	= 100,	/* 2000 */
 	};
 	time_t seconds_to_2000 = mktime(&time_2000);
-	time_t seconds_to_now = time(NULL);
+	time_t seconds_to_now = imagetool_get_source_date("mxsimage",
+							  time(NULL));

 	return seconds_to_now - seconds_to_2000;
 }
